 "name": "SEST Test: Polar North (Barents)",
 "description": "SEST PC TEST, not a campaign to play. Fog of war is off. March, the winter ice maximum. A Norwegian frigate in the Barents marginal ice east of Svalbard (78.4N 31E, about 50 % ice), the submarine Kobben under the pack 48 nm north (79.2N, about 70 %), a frigate off Bear Island and one in the ice-free Norwegian Sea, with Russian frigates closing from open water. Group N5 in the open central Barents Sea must cross the ice edge to reach a Russian picket in the pack (80.1N 43E). With SEST's sea ice on, the campaign map shows the ice edge and slows N5 in the ice, and the battle at the ice edge has visible pack ice, slowed ships, a submarine held under the ice and louder ice noise.",
